    <string name="input_method_preferences_dpad_description">accessibility dpad is Android 13+ only. ime dpad works on most apps, has reliability issues. fake dpad works on native UIs (usually). accessibility assisted ime dpad tries to balance fake/ime dpad.</string>
    <string name="input_method_preferences_keyboard_description">ime keyboard utilizes a keyboard service, accessibility keyboard only works on Android 13+ and only works on native text boxes.</string>
    <string name="input_method_preferences_media_description">ime media simulates real media buttons, notification service media controls the primary media session directly. not all apps use the media session api (but most do).</string>
    <string name="input_method_preferences_full_navigation_description">accessibility navigation uses global accessibility actions to simulate navigation events.</string>
    <string name="input_method_preferences_back_navigation_description">accessibility navigation uses a global accessibility action to simulate back navigation. ime navigation sends a back button key event to the application.</string>
    <string name="input_method_preferences_volume_description">accessibility volume directly controls the volume via audio manager. ime volume sends volume button key events to the application, which may be ignored and not work.</string>
    <string name="input_method_preferences_mouse_cursor_description">accessibility cursor draws a fake mouse cursor and simulates gestures for clicking/dragging. the device must have a touch screen or support fake touch for this to work (most real TVs don\'t)</string>
    <string name="input_method_preferences_activity_launcher_description">accessibility launcher uses accessibility service context to launch activities from the background.</string>
    <string name="input_method_preferences_power_description">accessibility power attempts to recreate power button functionality by checking the interactivity state, using accessibility actions, and using a wakeup overlay.</string>


